  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The review notes that while most of the evaluated studies are methodologically sound in their design, they frequently suffer from incomplete reporting of their eye-tracking procedures.",
      "what": "This systematic review synthesized 73 primary empirical studies and 3 reviews published between 2015 and 2025 to evaluate eye-tracking methodologies in urban public spaces. Using PRISMA guidelines, the study appraised research quality, mapped analytical pipelines for raw gaze data, and evaluated reporting completeness across devices, sample sizes, and spatial indicators.",
      "why": "It establishes a standardized methodological recommendation for transforming raw gaze data into spatially interpretable behavioral metrics, while identifying critical gaps in current research such as nighttime environments and culturally sensitive urban contexts."
